WEBVTT

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:00.976
and students in a different class
also nominated him for most ruthless,

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.684
even though they'd never
negotiated with him.

00:12:03.708 --> 00:12:05.851
A few years later,
I interviewed him about it,

00:12:05.875 --> 00:12:07.601
and he took it well.

00:12:07.625 --> 00:12:10.351
Heads up, I recorded this
before I even had an iPhone,

00:12:10.375 --> 00:12:12.143
so the quality's fuzzy.

00:12:12.167 --> 00:12:13.976
(Recording) JB: I won the Stanley Cup

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.518
and I've also won
a national championship in college,

00:12:16.542 --> 00:12:18.893
but that was by far
my highlight of my career --

00:12:18.917 --> 00:12:20.643
winning "most ruthless" negotiator.

00:12:20.667 --> 00:12:23.518
No, but how I won it was a situation

00:12:23.542 --> 00:12:26.518
where I wanted to win at all costs

00:12:26.542 --> 00:12:29.934
and really wanted just
to destroy my competitor.

00:12:29.958 --> 00:12:32.309
AG: When he graduated,
Jason got a management role